#. type: Title =
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/testing/component-tests.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Component tests"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/testing/component-tests.adoc
msgid ""
"xref:edge/implement.adoc[Implementing a Device] shows a first JUnit test. "
"This page describes the test framework in more detail. Components are tested "
"without running OSGi. The test framework in `+io.openems.edge.common+` "
"(package `+io.openems.edge.common.test+`) creates the component, sets "
"references by hand, activates it with a test configuration and replays "
"Cycles."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/testing/component-tests.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Running"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/testing/component-tests.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "./gradlew :io.openems.edge.controller.ess.balancing:test\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/testing/component-tests.adoc
msgid ""
"`+${testpath}+` (`+cnf/build.bnd+`) contains JUnit Jupiter and the Vintage "
"engine; both styles run. Rule from `+CLAUDE.md+`: keep the existing style in "
"existing files (many still use JUnit 4 with `+org.junit.Test+`), write new "
"test classes with Jupiter only if the bundle already uses Jupiter, and never "
"mix both in one file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/testing/component-tests.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Structure of a test"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-structure-of-a-test
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/testing/component-tests.adoc
msgid "Example from `+BalancingImplTest+`:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/testing/component-tests.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"new ControllerTest(new ControllerEssBalancingImpl())\n"
"        .addReference(\"ess\", new DummyManagedSymmetricEss(\"ess0\")\n"
"                .setPower(new DummyPower(0.3, 0.3, 0.1)))\n"
"        .addReference(\"meter\", new DummyElectricityMeter(\"meter0\"))\n"
"        .activate(MyConfig.create()\n"
"                .setId(\"ctrl0\")\n"
"                .setEssId(\"ess0\")\n"
"                .setMeterId(\"meter0\")\n"
"                .setTargetGridSetpoint(0)\n"
"                .build())\n"
"        .next(new TestCase()\n"
"                .input(\"ess0\", SymmetricEss.ChannelId.ACTIVE_POWER, 0)\n"
"                .input(\"meter0\", ElectricityMeter.ChannelId.ACTIVE_POWER, 20000)\n"
"                .output(\"ess0\", SET_ACTIVE_POWER_EQUALS, 6000))\n"
"        .next(new TestCase()\n"
"                .input(\"ess0\", SymmetricEss.ChannelId.ACTIVE_POWER, 0)\n"
"                .input(\"meter0\", ElectricityMeter.ChannelId.ACTIVE_POWER, 20000)\n"
"                .output(\"ess0\", SET_ACTIVE_POWER_EQUALS, 12000));\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/testing/component-tests.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Step\n"
"| Meaning\n"
"\n"
"| `+new ComponentTest(sut)+` / `+new ControllerTest(sut)+`\n"
"| framework around the component under test (`+sut+`). `+ControllerTest+` additionally calls `+run()+` in the Controller step.\n"
"| `+addReference(\"field\", object)+`\n"
"| sets a `+@Reference+` field via reflection. The name is the field name or, for setter references, the method name (e.g. `+\"setModbus\"+`).\n"
"| `+addComponent(object)+`\n"
"| registers another component without assigning it to a field; if a `+DummyComponentManager+` is set as a reference, it is also entered there\n"
"| `+activate(config)+`\n"
"| calls the `+@Activate+` method with the test configuration; if `+activate()+` changes the configuration (e.g. reference filter), the component is deactivated and reactivated as in OSGi\n"
"| `+next(testCase)+`\n"
"| runs through one Cycle; `+next(testCase, n)+` repeats it n times\n"
"| `+deactivate()+`\n"
"| calls `+@Deactivate+`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/testing/component-tests.adoc
msgid ""
"In the example, the setpoint rises from Cycle to Cycle (6000, 12000 …) "
"because the setpoint is set “with filter” and the PID filter of "
"`+DummyPower(0.3, 0.3, 0.1)+` takes effect (p, i, d)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/testing/component-tests.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sequence of `+next()+`"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-sequence-of-next
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/testing/component-tests.adoc
msgid ""
"The order corresponds to the real Cycle (see xref:development/fundamentals/"
"cycle-and-ess-power.adoc[Cycle]):"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-sequence-of-next
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/testing/component-tests.adoc
msgid "Apply time leap (`+timeleap+`)"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-sequence-of-next
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/testing/component-tests.adoc
msgid ""
"Event BEFORE_PROCESS_IMAGE, then switch the Process Image of the component "
"under test"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-sequence-of-next
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/testing/component-tests.adoc
msgid ""
"**Set inputs**: the values from `+input(…)+` are set and immediately adopted "
"into the Process Image. They are thus already visible via `+value()+` in the "
"same test Cycle."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-sequence-of-next
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/testing/component-tests.adoc
msgid ""
"Events AFTER_PROCESS_IMAGE, BEFORE_CONTROLLERS, execute Controllers, "
"AFTER_CONTROLLERS, BEFORE_WRITE, EXECUTE_WRITE, AFTER_WRITE"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-sequence-of-next
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/testing/component-tests.adoc
msgid "**Check outputs**"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-sequence-of-next
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/testing/component-tests.adoc
msgid "How `+output(…)+` checks:"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-sequence-of-next
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/testing/component-tests.adoc
msgid ""
"for write-channels the **next write value** (`+getNextWriteValueAndReset()"
"+`),"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-sequence-of-next
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/testing/component-tests.adoc
msgid ""
"for other Channels the **next value** (`+getNextValue()+`), i.e. the value "
"that the component set in this Cycle,"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-sequence-of-next
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/testing/component-tests.adoc
msgid ""
"`+outputReadValue(…)+` instead checks `+value()+` from the current Process "
"Image."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-sequence-of-next
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/testing/component-tests.adoc
msgid ""
"For your own checks, there are callbacks per phase, e.g. "
"`+onBeforeProcessImage(…)+`, `+onAfterControllers…+`, `+onAfterWrite…+`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/testing/component-tests.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Controlling time"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-controlling-time
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/testing/component-tests.adoc
msgid ""
"Components that work with time get the clock via "
"`+componentManager.getClock()+`. In the test:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/testing/component-tests.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"final var clock = createDummyClock();     // TimeLeapClock, start 2020-01-01 00:00 UTC\n"
"new ControllerTest(new MyControllerImpl())\n"
"        .addReference(\"componentManager\", new DummyComponentManager(clock))\n"
"        ...\n"
"        .next(new TestCase()\n"
"                .timeleap(clock, 15, ChronoUnit.MINUTES)\n"
"                .output(...));\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/testing/component-tests.adoc
msgid ""
"`+createDummyClock()+` is in `+io.openems.common.test.TestUtils+`. This "
"allows delays, day changes or quarter-hour grids, for example, to be tested "
"without waiting."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/testing/component-tests.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Strict mode"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-strict-mode
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/testing/component-tests.adoc
msgid ""
"`+new TestCase().activateStrictMode()+` requires that all Channels of the "
"tested component appear in inputs or outputs. Channels that you deliberately "
"do not check are excluded with `+withIgnoredChannelsForStrictMode(…)+`. This "
"finds forgotten or unexpectedly set Channels."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/testing/component-tests.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Dummy components"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/testing/component-tests.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Class\n"
"| Bundle (package `+…test+`)\n"
"| Purpose\n"
"\n"
"| `+DummyManagedSymmetricEss+`, `+DummySymmetricEss+`, `+DummyHybridEss+`, `+DummyMetaEss+`\n"
"| `+io.openems.edge.ess.api+`\n"
"| ESS\n"
"| `+DummyPower+`\n"
"| `+io.openems.edge.ess.api+`\n"
"| ESS Power, optionally with PID parameters or maximum power\n"
"| `+DummyElectricityMeter+`, `+DummySinglePhaseElectricityMeter+`\n"
"| `+io.openems.edge.meter.api+`\n"
"| meters\n"
"| `+DummyComponentManager+`, `+DummyCycle+`, `+DummyMeta+`, `+DummyEventAdmin+`\n"
"| `+io.openems.edge.common+`\n"
"| core services\n"
"| `+DummyConfigurationAdmin+`, `+TimeLeapClock+`\n"
"| `+io.openems.common+`\n"
"| Configuration Admin, controllable clock\n"
"| `+DummyModbusBridge+`\n"
"| `+io.openems.edge.bridge.modbus+`\n"
"| Modbus Bridge with predefined registers\n"
"| `+DummyScheduler+`\n"
"| `+io.openems.edge.scheduler.api+`\n"
"| Scheduler\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/testing/component-tests.adoc
msgid ""
"The dummy classes are in the `+src+` folder of the API bundles (package `+…"
"test+`) so that other bundles can use them in tests. The API bundle must be "
"in the `+-buildpath+` or `+-testpath+` for this."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/testing/component-tests.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Testing Modbus drivers"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/testing/component-tests.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"new ComponentTest(new MeterJanitzaUmg96rmeImpl())\n"
"        .addReference(\"setModbus\", new DummyModbusBridge(\"modbus0\")\n"
"                .withRegisters(19000,\n"
"                        0x3F80, 0x0000,      // VOLTAGE_L1 = 1.0f\n"
"                        0x3F80, 0x0000,      // VOLTAGE_L2\n"
"                        ...))\n"
"        .activate(MyConfig.create()\n"
"                .setId(\"meter0\")\n"
"                .setModbusId(\"modbus0\")\n"
"                .setType(GRID)\n"
"                .build())\n"
"        .next(new TestCase()\n"
"                .output(ElectricityMeter.ChannelId.VOLTAGE_L1, 1000));\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/testing/component-tests.adoc
msgid ""
"`+DummyModbusBridge+` offers, among others, `+withRegister(address, value)"
"+`, `+withRegisters(start, values…)+`, `+withRegistersFloat32(start, floats…)"
"+` and `+withInputRegister(s)+` for FC4. This allows register assignment, "
"word order and converters to be checked without a device."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/testing/component-tests.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "MyConfig"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-myconfig
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/testing/component-tests.adoc
msgid ""
"Each test has a class `+MyConfig extends AbstractComponentConfig implements "
"Config+` with a builder. It implements all methods of the Config annotation "
"and returns the values from the builder. `+AbstractComponentConfig+` "
"(`+io.openems.common.test+`) provides the property structure that "
"`+activate()+` expects. New Config fields must also be added to "
"`+MyConfig+`, otherwise the test cannot be compiled."
msgstr ""
